{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfcTFrNHrGKhtvWASpeRh", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Banker's rounding (round-half-to-even) is a tie-breaking rule for rounding. Normal values round to the nearest number as usual. Only exact halves are special: they round to the nearest **even** digit.\n\n- 2.5 \u2192 2\n- 3.5 \u2192 4\n- 0.125 \u2192 0.12 (to 2 places)\n- 0.135 \u2192 0.14\n- 2.4 \u2192 2 and 2.6 \u2192 3 (not ties, so normal)\n\n**Why accountants like it**\n\n1. **It removes systematic bias.** \"Round half up\" always pushes ties upward. Over thousands of transactions, that adds a small but consistent upward drift. With round-half-even, ties go up about half the time and down about half the time, so the errors tend to cancel.\n2. **Totals stay closer to the truth.** When you round many line items (tax, interest, allocations) and sum them, the total is less likely to drift from the sum of the unrounded values.\n3. **It's fair to both parties.** Neither the payer nor the payee is consistently favored by the rounding.\n4. **It's a standard.** IEEE 754 uses it as the default rounding mode, and many financial and accounting rules specify it. That makes results reproducible and auditable across systems.\n\n**Caveats**\n\n- The benefit only shows up across many values. For a single number, it's no more accurate than round-half-up.\n- Ties are only common when the data has limited precision, such as values already rounded to a few decimals. With long random decimals, exact ties are rare.\n- Some jurisdictions or contracts require round-half-up, so check the governing rule.\n- In floating point, many \"ties\" like 2.675 aren't exact ties because of binary representation. Use a decimal type, for example Python's `decimal.ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, for money.\n\nThis matches what your project already does. The EngramDB decision memory says tax amounts use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, as agreed with the finance team in March 2026."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7828, "cache_read_input_tokens": 16975, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7828}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "6188d5fd-276f-4b22-80a9-55223f442fc6", "uuid": "05eff50a-43cb-426b-aa13-47b24d2d8ed9", "timestamp": "2026-10-02T00:20:37.366Z", "request_id": "req_011CfcTFrAddRBZ46UZPEoaV"}
